WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.264
Telemetry quality determines whether collected data can support a decision.

00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:07.179
Completeness asks whether required activity is represented.

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:10.510
Accuracy asks whether fields describe the correct event.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.425
Reliable asset mapping, units, identities, protocol decoding,

00:00:13.425 --> 00:00:16.756
and status values are all part of quality.

00:00:16.756 --> 00:00:19.254
Time synchronization is essential for correlation.

00:00:19.254 --> 00:00:20.920
Controllers, servers, remote sites,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.084
and security platforms may use different clocks or time zones.

00:00:25.084 --> 00:00:27.166
Record clock sources, expected drift,

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:32.163
and timestamp meaning so investigators can build a defensible sequence of events.

00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:35.911
Retention should reflect investigation needs, source volume, operational cycles,

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.993
legal constraints, and storage cost.

00:00:37.993 --> 00:00:42.989
Normalization makes data searchable across systems, but it must preserve source detail.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.986
Overly broad parsing can hide important industrial fields or produce misleading values.

00:00:47.986 --> 00:00:52.983
Coverage is the portion of important activity that the program can observe.

00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:57.563
Gaps may include serial networks, encrypted sessions, dormant assets, unsupported devices,

00:00:57.563 --> 00:01:00.478
local engineering actions, or sites without sensors.

00:01:00.478 --> 00:01:05.891
A coverage map should connect use cases to sources and state limitations openly.

00:01:05.891 --> 00:01:10.055
Noisy data creates a different gap between collection and visibility.

00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:13.803
Duplicate alarms, unstable asset names, missing fields, parser errors,

00:01:13.803 --> 00:01:16.302
and excessive low-value events consume attention.

00:01:16.302 --> 00:01:21.298
Monitor source health, event rate, delay, loss, schema changes, and enrichment success.

00:01:21.298 --> 00:01:22.964
Quality control is continuous.

00:01:22.964 --> 00:01:27.128
Assign source owners, test changes, investigate collection failures, protect integrity,

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:31.292
and review whether retained data still supports operations and security.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:37.122
A large archive is not a telemetry program unless teams can find, trust, interpret,

00:01:37.122 --> 00:01:39.620
and act on what it contains.
